WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.987 --> 00:00:02.838
- When he goes out and actually
deploys to chase something,

00:00:02.838 --> 00:00:04.747
it looks like a missile launch.

00:00:04.747 --> 00:00:06.760
I just open up the back
door and he jumps out.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:08.501
It's a lot of fun.

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:10.988
Piper is the only dog
working at this airport,

00:00:10.988 --> 00:00:12.829
and there's actually
only a handful of dogs

00:00:12.829 --> 00:00:15.357
working at airports around the country.

00:00:15.357 --> 00:00:17.440
It's a pretty rare thing.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:23.937
I am Brian Edwards.

00:00:23.937 --> 00:00:25.898
Piper and I work at the
Cherry Capital Airport

00:00:25.898 --> 00:00:28.148
in Traverse City, Michigan.

00:00:30.709 --> 00:00:32.717
Piper is a Border Collie.

00:00:32.717 --> 00:00:35.949
Piper's prime function
here is wildlife control.

00:00:35.949 --> 00:00:38.405
Primarily, Piper is
going to be chasing away

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:40.966
large waterfowl like ducks and geese.

00:00:40.966 --> 00:00:44.077
In the wintertime, it actually
chases away the snowy owl,

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.187
and then in the summertime,

00:00:45.187 --> 00:00:48.549
it's basically seagulls and crows.

00:00:48.549 --> 00:00:51.098
Birds can cause a lot of
different types of damage.

00:00:51.098 --> 00:00:52.527
Most bird strikes are with smaller

00:00:52.527 --> 00:00:54.847
types of birds that
might just cause dents,

00:00:54.847 --> 00:00:56.367
but if the bird is large enough

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:57.796
and is ingested into an engine,

00:00:57.796 --> 00:00:59.509
that can cause serious failure

00:00:59.509 --> 00:01:02.092
like the Miracle on the Hudson.

00:01:04.349 --> 00:01:05.997
Training specifically for us took

00:01:05.997 --> 00:01:08.138
about a year, year and a half.

00:01:08.138 --> 00:01:09.837
So, the way that we've trained is that

00:01:09.837 --> 00:01:12.749
anytime I deploy Piper out of the truck,

00:01:12.749 --> 00:01:14.538
he doesn't just run away from the truck,

00:01:14.538 --> 00:01:17.117
he always runs the
direction we were traveling.

00:01:17.117 --> 00:01:20.215
A lot of times I deploy him
when the vehicle is moving,

00:01:20.215 --> 00:01:21.427
so that's just the way that we trained.

00:01:21.427 --> 00:01:23.418
A lot of times I try to get him to see

00:01:23.418 --> 00:01:25.622
what it is he's gonna chase first.

00:01:25.622 --> 00:01:29.431
The goggles, or the Rec Specs,
serve two purposes for him.

00:01:29.431 --> 00:01:32.366
One, they're UV protectant
so they protect his eyes,

00:01:32.366 --> 00:01:35.355
and number two, they're
safety goggles, basically.

00:01:35.355 --> 00:01:36.636
It's one of those things
that if he wants to

00:01:36.636 --> 00:01:40.636
go out and work or have
fun, he's gotta wear it.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.713
Yeah, good boy!

00:01:43.713 --> 00:01:45.534
Go get ‘em, buddy! Go get em!

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:48.214
Dogs are really useful
for wildlife control

00:01:48.214 --> 00:01:51.593
because specifically Border
Collies, it's in their blood.

00:01:51.593 --> 00:01:54.713
Eventually, the goal is to train the birds

00:01:54.713 --> 00:01:56.702
and other animals that
they don't wanna be here

00:01:56.702 --> 00:01:58.564
because there's a predator in town,

00:01:58.564 --> 00:02:01.764
something that's gonna keep
harassing them all the time.

00:02:01.764 --> 00:02:04.705
Piper's been with me at the
airport for almost three years.

00:02:04.705 --> 00:02:06.745
He's pretty much with me all the time.

00:02:06.745 --> 00:02:08.374
I don't think Piper sees it as work,

00:02:08.374 --> 00:02:12.541
I think it's all play to him,
which is what we want, right?

00:02:15.741 --> 00:02:17.275
The best thing personally with Piper,

00:02:17.275 --> 00:02:21.125
and it's been this way
before we started working,

00:02:21.125 --> 00:02:22.494
he's got a mind of his own.

00:02:22.494 --> 00:02:24.635
I talk to him like I would
talk to anybody else.

00:02:24.635 --> 00:02:25.638
He's my bro.

00:02:25.638 --> 00:02:26.758
Does it get any better than that?

00:02:26.758 --> 00:02:28.987
I get to work with my
best friend every day,

00:02:28.987 --> 00:02:30.566
I'm extremely proud of him,

00:02:30.566 --> 00:02:31.766
I couldn't ask for anything more.

00:02:31.766 --> 00:02:34.683
(orchestral music)

